{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For a curse of Elohim is hanged.</b> Because he blessed the Name, and according to the plain sense: that Elohim acts and the curse comes upon every place near the hanged one. And it has a secret cleaving to the soul; therefore, <i>you shall not defile your land</i>. And this pericope is juxtaposed because of war, for at first <i>When you go out</i> [Deut. 21:10], and behold Gibeon proves, for the rule <i>you shall not leave [him hanging] overnight</i> is not for the honor of the dead but for the honor of the land, for the law of the uncircumcised and the Israelites is equal:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The phrase 'because he blessed the Name' appears to be elliptical; read hyper-literally as printed. The bracketed [איננו] follows the apparatus in מ״ח מ״ז (vol. 48, p. 47); translated as printed with brackets."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:16.570287394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}